e user might have intended to run a setup script but forgot to include it. Alternatively, it could be a leftover from a previous deployment. \n\nI need to confirm if there\'s any other configuration that might affect this. Checking the deployment or replica set for the custom-service could help. But since I can\'t use the get_operations or get_services tools here, maybe I should check the deployment YAML. However, the available tools don\'t include getting deployments directly. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the init container is part of the deployment\'s spec. Since the user has access to kubectl, they can check the deployment\'s YAML. But in the current tools, the only way is through kubectl commands. \n\nWait, the user already used kubectl get pod -o yaml. The spec shows the init container\'s command. So the problem is definitely the init container\'s command. The root cause is that the init container is configured to sleep indefinitely, which prevents the pod from initializing and starting the main container. \n\nTherefore, the faulty component is the custom-service\'s init container with the sleep infinity command. The fix would involve correcting the init container\'s command to perform the necessary setup tasks or removing it if it\'s not required. \n\nSo, the final answer should state that the root cause is the init container in the custom-service pod being configured to sleep indefinitely, which blocks the pod from initializing and starting the main container.\n</think>\n\nsubmit_tool\n{"ans": "The root cause of the failure is the `custom-service` pod\'s init container (`hang-init`) being configured to run `sleep infinity`, which intentionally blocks the pod from initializing. This prevents the main container (`custom-service-main`) from starting, leaving the pod in a `Pending` state. The init container\'s infinite sleep suggests a misconfiguration or an intentional pause, likely due to an unimplemented setup task or a deployment error. The faulty component is the `hang-init` init container in the `custom-service` deployment, which must be corrected or removed to allow the pod to proceed with initialization."}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'refusal': None, 'reasoning': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': Usage(completion_tokens=806, prompt_tokens=7352, total_tokens=8158, completion_tokens_details=None, prompt_tokens_details=None), 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfd08-79d7-7e30-95db-06f76496d450-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 7352, 'output_tokens': 806, 'total_tokens': 8158}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='de617b1a-bdf2-46fe-8f74-ad1a0c090d2e')]]
